	Forest
	<br>
	<<lakeicon>><<link [[Ride your bike to the lake|Bike Ride]]>><<set $bikeDestination to "lake">><<set $bikeEndCategory to "lake">><</link>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>

<<cancelBike>>

:: Bike Ride
<<effects>>
<<if $bikeStartCategory is "lake">>
 <<if $rng lte 70>>
    <<if Weather.dayState is "night">>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
            Black rain pours down, making the road slick. Your bike's tires send up sprays of water as you carefully navigate the winding forest path.
        <<elseif Weather.isSnow>>
            Dark snow falls silently, covering the road in a thin layer. Your tires crunch through the fresh snow as you cautiously push forward through the quiet forest.
        <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
            The stars are faint but visible above the trees, offering just enough light to guide your way as you ride through the stillness of the forest.
        <<else>>
            Thick clouds blanket the sky, making the night even darker as your bike light struggles to illuminate the path ahead.
        <</if>>
    <<elseif Weather.dayState is "dusk">>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
            Evening rain glistens on the smooth road, creating a reflective surface as you ride cautiously along the forest path.
        <<elseif Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
            Snow begins to settle for the night, creating a soft crunch beneath your tires as dusk fades to night.
        <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
            The setting sun casts a warm, golden light over the road, guiding your way as the day comes to an end.
        <<else>>
            Heavy clouds gather overhead, darkening the forest road as the light fades.
        <</if>>
    <<elseif Weather.dayState is "dawn">>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
            The early morning rain shimmers on the road, and your bike kicks up small sprays of water as you ride through the fresh, cool air.
        <<elseif Weather.isSnow>>
            A blanket of snow reflects the dawn's light, turning the road into a crisp, white path as you make your way through the peaceful forest.
        <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
            The sun rises between the trees, casting long shadows across the road, offering a serene start to your ride.
        <<else>>
            The sky is thick with clouds, turning the morning gray and cool as you pedal forward through the forest.
        <</if>>
    <<else>>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
            The rain-soaked road glistens beneath your tires, the path ahead slick but manageable as you push through the rain.
        <<elseif Weather.isSnow>>
            The road is lightly dusted with snow, your tires crunching softly as you ride through the winter landscape.
        <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
            The sun shines weakly through the trees, its pale light reflecting off the smooth road as you continue your journey.
        <<else>>
            Clouds hang low and heavy, dimming the day and casting a cold light over the forest.
        <</if>>
    <</if>>
        <<if Weather.dayState is "night">>
            Riding through the dark forest keeps you tense the whole way, and every unseen bump jars the bike. <<stress 2>><<gstress>><<set $bikeDurability -= 1>><br><br>
        <</if>>
        <<if Time.season is "spring">>
            <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
                Mud washed down over the forest road cakes your tires and forces you to brake often, leaving your legs aching and the chain grinding. <<stress 2>><<gstress>><<tiredness 3>><<gtiredness>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 2>>
            <<else>>
                The thaw-softened forest path is full of hidden ruts that jolt the frame and wear at your nerves. <<tiredness 5>><<gtiredness>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 1>>
            <</if>>
        <<elseif Time.season is "summer">>
            <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
                Warm rain turns patches of moss into slick traps, forcing you to keep your speed down and your grip tight.<<tiredness 5>><<gtiredness>><<set $bikeDurability -= 3>>
            <<else>>
                The humid forest air and constant insects wear on you even without a serious incident.<<tiredness 3>><<gtiredness>>
            <</if>>
        <<elseif Time.season is "autumn">>
            Wet leaves and cold damp work their way into every part of the ride, leaving you sore and forcing extra wear on the brakes. <<stress 2>><<gstress>> <<tiredness 3>><<gtiredness>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 2>>
        <<elseif Time.season is "winter">>
            The cold stiffens your hands and every icy patch forces you to ride with caution. <<stress 2>><<gstress>><<tiredness 3>><<gtiredness>><<set $bikeDurability -= 3>>
        <</if>>
        <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain" or $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain">>
         Birds are singing in the trees while riding your bike through the forest. You notice a big swarm of flies directly ahead and swirl a little bit to the left to avoid it. <<stress -5>><<lstress>>
        <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain" or $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain">>
        While riding your bike through the forest your attention is taken away by a weird noise to your right. You turn your head back to the road after trying to find the source and something flies straight in your mouth and nose. 
        Spitting out the thing that flew in your mouth and rubbing your now itchy nose you look at the road behind you. A swarm of flies are buzzing over the road you just passed. <<stress 10>><<ggstress>><<arousal -200>><<larousal>>
         <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation is "rain" or $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
        While rain pours down from above, you pedal through the forest making your way to your destination. Visibility is low and the road is slippery and when a sharp turn comes around you almost get into a slide. 
        Luckily you can stay in control of your bike and avoid slipping into the stream next to you. <<stress -2>><<lstress>> <<control 1>> <<gcontrol>>
        <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation is "rain" or $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
        While riding your bike through the forest rain pours out of the clouds above. 
        The rain makes it hard to see what lies ahead and when a small rock on the road makes you lose control, you fall from your bike into the stream next to you. 
         <br>
        Luckily you are still in one piece but dry you are not. <<pain 3>><<gpain>><<control -2>><<lcontrol>><<trauma 1>><<gtrauma>> <<upperwet 100>> <<underupperwet 100>> <<lowerwet 100>> <<underlowerwet 100>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 25>>
        <<elseif $rng gte 86 and $rng lte 89 and (Time.season is "summer" or Time.season is "spring") and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain">>
        A warm breeze carries the scent of wildflowers as you coast downhill through the forest. The ride is smooth and the air feels good in your lungs. You arrive feeling refreshed. <<stress -4>><<llstress>> <<control 1>><<gcontrol>>
        <<elseif $rng gte 86 and $rng lte 89 and (Time.season is "summer" or Time.season is "spring") and Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
        Spring rain hammers the forest canopy, and a branch weakened by the downpour snaps and falls across the path. You brake hard and skid sideways, your knee slamming into the frame. <<stress 6>><<ggstress>> <<pain 3>><<gpain>><<set $bikeDurability -= 18>>
        <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 80 and Time.season is "autumn">>
        Damp, rotting leaves carpet the forest trail, turning every curve treacherous. Your tires slip on the mulch and you fight to keep the handlebars steady, arriving rattled but upright. <<tiredness 6>><<gtiredness>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 5>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 81 and $rng lte 89 and Time.season is "autumn">>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
        Autumn rain and fallen leaves conspire to turn the forest path into a skating rink. Your front tire locks on a mat of wet leaves and you skid sideways, slamming your knee into a tree root. <<stress 6>><<ggstress>> <<pain 4>><<gpain>>
        <<else>>
        A hidden branch snaps under your front tire and jams the wheel. You flip over the handlebars and tumble across the leaf-strewn path. <<stress 5>><<ggstress>> <<pain 3>><<ggpain>> <<control -1>><<lcontrol>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 15>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "autumn">>
        The trail is buried under sodden leaves. Without warning your tires lose all grip on a steep downhill and you crash hard into the underbrush, your bike crunching beneath you. You lie there, shaking, heart pounding. <<pain 6>><<gpain>> <<trauma 3>><<gtrauma>> <<control -3>><<lcontrol>><<set $bikeDurability -= 30>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 80 and Time.season is "winter">>
        <<if Weather.isSnow>>
        Snow covers the forest trail, hiding roots and rocks. You push through slowly, your legs burning from the effort and your fingers numb on the grips. <<tiredness 8>><<ggtiredness>><<set $bikeDurability -= 5>>
        <<else>>
        A thin layer of frost coats the forest path. Every pedal stroke feels uncertain, your tires barely gripping the frozen earth. <<stress 4>><<gstress>> <<tiredness 5>><<gtiredness>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 81 and $rng lte 89 and Time.season is "winter">>
        <<if Weather.isSnow>>
        Deep snow hides a frozen rut in the trail. Your front wheel drops in and twists sharply, throwing you sideways into a snowbank. The cold bites into your exposed skin immediately. <<stress 6>><<ggstress>> <<pain 4>><<gpain>> <<control -2>><<lcontrol>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 20>> <<upperwet 50>> <<lowerwet 50>>
        <<else>>
        Black ice lurks beneath a layer of dead leaves. Your bike slides out from under you without warning, slamming you onto the frozen ground. <<stress 6>><<ggstress>> <<pain 5>><<gpain>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 20>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "winter">>
        The trail is an icy hellscape. Your tires hit a patch of solid ice on a curve and you lose control completely, crashing through frozen brush and sliding down an embankment. The impact drives the air from your lungs. Your bike frame groans from the abuse.<<pain 8>><<ggpain>> <<trauma 5>><<gtrauma>> <<control -4>><<lcontrol>><<set $bikeDurability -= 35>>
    <</if>>

<<elseif $bikeStartCategory is "left" or $bikeStartCategory is "mid" or $bikeStartCategory is "right">>
    <<if $rng lte 70>>
        <<if Weather.dayState is "night">>
            <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
                Rainwater streams down the streets, reflecting the dim streetlights as your tires send up sprays of water with each turn.
            <<elseif Weather.isSnow>>
                Snow blankets the town, the roads slick under your tires as you ride past quiet shops and homes.
            <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
                The stars are faint in the sky above, with the streetlights providing most of the light as you ride through the sleeping town.
            <<else>>
                Thick clouds blanket the sky, blocking out any natural light as your bike light flickers on the road ahead.
            <</if>>
        <<elseif Weather.dayState is "dusk">>
            <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
                The evening rain turns the town roads into glistening paths, and your cautious riding keeps you steady as you move through the wet streets.
            <<elseif Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
                Snow begins to accumulate, softening the sound of your tires as you ride through the peaceful, snow-covered town.
            <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
                The sun dips below the rooftops, casting long shadows across the roads as you make your way through the town.
            <<else>>
                Dark clouds gather, creating an overcast sky that hides the last rays of daylight as you navigate the town streets.
            <</if>>
        <<elseif Weather.dayState is "dawn">>
            <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
                The dawn's light glimmers off the rain-soaked streets, and your tires splash through the shallow puddles as you ride through the quiet town.
            <<elseif Weather.isSnow>>
                Snow reflects the morning light, covering the streets in a blanket of white as your tires leave tracks behind.
            <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
                The sun rises over the rooftops, lighting up the town as you pedal through the calm streets.
            <<else>>
                A thick layer of clouds turns the sky gray, casting a cool light over the streets as you ride through the early morning.
            <</if>>
        <<else>>
            <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
                Rain pours down, soaking the town streets as your clothes grow heavier with each passing minute.
            <<elseif Weather.isSnow>>
                The streets are coated in snow, making your ride slower as your tires struggle to grip the frosty ground.
            <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
                The sun shines weakly, offering little warmth as you ride through the chilly town.
            <<else>>
                Overcast clouds cover the sky, casting a dull, gray light over the town streets as you ride.
            <</if>>
        <</if>>
        <<if Weather.dayState is "night">>
            Riding through town after dark keeps you keyed up, and every sudden headlight makes you clutch the handlebars tighter. <<stress 1>><<gstress>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 1>><br><br>
        <</if>>
        <<if Time.season is "spring">>
            <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
                Overflowing gutters and slick painted road markings keep forcing you to brake and correct your line. <<control -1>><<lcontrol>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 2>>
            <<else>>
                Stop-start traffic and potholes left by the thaw make for a bumpier ride than you'd like. <<tiredness 5>><<gtiredness>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 1>>
            <</if>>
        <<elseif Time.season is "summer">>
            <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
                Rainwater hides cracks in the road and turns every corner into a cautious crawl. <<stress 2>><<gstress>> <<tiredness 5>><<gtiredness>><<set $bikeDurability -= 2>>
            <<else>>
                Heat rising from the pavement and the constant need to watch traffic leave you more worn than refreshed.<<tiredness 4>><<gtiredness>>
            <</if>>
        <<elseif Time.season is "autumn">>
            Gusts between the buildings and wet debris along the curb keep you on edge for the whole ride. <<stress 2>><<gstress>>
        <<elseif Time.season is "winter">>
            The cold numbs your hands and the streets stay slick enough that you never quite relax. <<stress 2>><<gstress>><<set $bikeDurability -= 2>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain" or $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain">>
        While riding with your bike through town a swarm of small flies crosses your path. Luckily you saw them on time and can dodge out of the way. <<stress -2>><<lstress>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain" or $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain">>
         You enjoy the ride through town when suddenly a swarm of little flies crosses your path. Too late you realise it and while riding through them, you swallow a couple of them. 
         One of the flies bangs straight into your eye. You spit out some that entered your mouth and with one hand you try to rub the fly out of your eye. <<stress 3>><<gstress>><<arousal -200>><<larousal>><<pain 2>><<gpain>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation is "rain" or $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
        Rain is pouring out of the sky while you ride to your destination. The water flows fast through the gutters which are having a difficult time to handle it all. 
        A car passes by at high speed and splashes water to all sides. Luckily the biggest splash misses you by a few inches. <<stress -4>><<lstress>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation is "rain" or $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
    Rain pours out of the clouds above you while pedaling with your bike to your destination. The town drains are having a difficult time to handle all the rain and the road is starting to disappear under the water. 
    Suddenly a car speeds by at high velocity and a big splash of water hits you in the side, drenching you from top to toe and shoving the bike a lane over. <<stress 6>><<ggstress>><<control -2>><<lcontrol>> <<upperwet 30>> <<underupperwet 30>> <<lowerwet 30>> <<underlowerwet 30>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 5>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 86 and $rng lte 89 and (Time.season is "summer" or Time.season is "spring") and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain">>
        You catch every green light and the streets are clear. A cool breeze takes the edge off the heat. You arrive in good spirits, feeling sharp and alert. <<stress -3>><<lstress>> <<control 1>><<gcontrol>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 86 and $rng lte 89 and (Time.season is "summer" or Time.season is "spring") and Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
        A sudden downpour floods the gutters. Your tire catches a submerged pothole and you wrench the handlebars to stay upright, tweaking your wrist in the process. Water sprays up, soaking your legs. <<stress 5>><<gstress>> <<lowerwet 60>> <<underlowerwet 60>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 12>> <<control -1>><<lcontrol>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 80 and Time.season is "autumn">>
        Wet leaves have piled up along the curb, spilling onto the road. You swerve around the worst of it but your back tire fishtails, and the sudden jolt of adrenaline leaves you tense for the rest of the ride. <<stress 4>><<gstress>><<set $bikeDurability -= 5>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 81 and $rng lte 89 and Time.season is "autumn">>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
        Autumn rain has turned the leaf-covered streets into a hazard. Your front tire slides on a patch of wet leaves as you round a corner and you crash into the curb, scraping your hands and knees on the pavement. <<stress 6>><<ggstress>> <<pain 4>><<ggpain>><<set $bikeDurability -= 15>> <<upperwet 40>> <<lowerwet 40>>
        <<else>>
        A strong autumn gust funnels between the buildings and hits you broadside. You fight the handlebars but your tire catches a storm drain and you tumble onto the road. A car honks and swerves around you. <<stress 7>><<ggstress>> <<pain 3>><<ggpain>> <<trauma 2>><<gtrauma>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 15>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "autumn">>
        A gust of wind catches you at an intersection just as a car runs a puddle at full speed. The wave of filthy water hits you square in the face, blinding you. You crash into a parked car, denting your frame and leaving you sprawled on the wet pavement, shaken and bruised. <<pain 6>><<gpain>> <<trauma 4>><<ggtrauma>><<upperwet 20>> <<underupperwet 20>> <<lowerwet 20>> <<underlowerwet 20>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 30>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 80 and Time.season is "winter">>
        <<if Weather.isSnow>>
        Snow has been packed into ice by foot traffic on the road shoulders. You ride slowly, teeth chattering, muscles clenched against the cold. <<tiredness 6>><<gtiredness>>
        <<else>>
        Frost makes the town streets deceptively slippery. You white-knuckle the handlebars the entire way, arriving stiff and anxious. <<stress 5>><<gstress>> <<tiredness 5>><<gtiredness>><<set $bikeDurability -= 5>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 81 and $rng lte 89 and Time.season is "winter">>
        <<if Weather.isSnow>>
        Slush and compacted snow hide a pothole. Your front wheel drops in hard, buckling slightly, and you topple sideways into a dirty snowbank. Freezing water soaks through your clothes instantly. <<stress 6>><<ggstress>> <<pain 4>><<ggpain>><<set $bikeDurability -= 20>> <<upperwet 70>> <<underupperwet 70>> <<lowerwet 70>> <<underlowerwet 70>>
        <<else>>
        A patch of black ice at a crosswalk sends your bike sliding. You go down hard on the frozen tarmac, the impact rattling your teeth and scraping your palms raw. <<stress 7>><<ggstress>> <<pain 5>><<gpain>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 20>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "winter">>
        The streets are a treacherous maze of ice and frozen slush. As you round a corner, your tires lose all purchase on a sheet of ice. You slide helplessly into the path of oncoming traffic. A car screeches to a halt inches from you as you crash into the gutter, your bike crumpling beneath you. Your heart pounds so hard it hurts. <<stress 10>><<ggstress>> <<pain 7>><<ggpain>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 35>>
    <</if>>

<<elseif $bikeStartCategory is "farm">>
    <<if $rng lte 70>>
    <<if Weather.dayState is "night">>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
            Rain falls heavily, and the rural road gleams under your bike light as water runs in small streams along the smooth surface.
        <<elseif Weather.isSnow>>
            Snow drifts across the farmlands, covering the road in a thick blanket as your tires crunch through the accumulating snow.
        <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
            The stars stretch across the wide-open sky, with your bike rolling smoothly down the road as you ride through the silent countryside.
        <<else>>
            Thick clouds obscure the night sky, making it even darker as your bike light struggles to cut through the shadows on the rural road.
        <</if>>
    <<elseif Weather.dayState is "dusk">>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
            Rain sparkles on the rural road as the sun sets, and your tires send up small sprays of water as you pedal through the farmlands.
        <<elseif Weather.precipitation is "snow">>
            Snow begins to cover the fields and road, and your bike crunches through it as the light fades from the sky.
        <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
            The sun sets over the farmlands, casting long shadows over the fields as you pedal through the tranquil landscape.
        <<else>>
            A thick layer of clouds gathers above, dimming the sky as night approaches over the farmlands.
        <</if>>
    <<elseif Weather.dayState is "dawn">>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
            Morning rain glimmers on the rural road as the sun begins to rise, your tires splashing through the wet surface.
        <<elseif Weather.isSnow>>
            Snow covers the farmlands, reflecting the early morning light as your tires leave deep tracks in the soft snow.
        <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
            The sun rises over the distant hills, lighting up the road and fields as you ride through the serene farmlands.
        <<else>>
            Overcast clouds cover the morning sky, casting a gray light over the countryside as you ride through the farmlands.
        <</if>>
    <<else>>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
            Rain pours down onto the farmlands, the road slick but still manageable as you push forward through the countryside.
        <<elseif Weather.isSnow>>
            Snow blankets the fields and the road, your tires struggling to push through the deep drifts.
        <<elseif !Weather.isOvercast>>
            The sun shines weakly over the farmlands, its light doing little to ease the cold as you ride through the open landscape.
        <<else>>
            Overcast clouds hang low in the sky, casting a dull light over the farmlands as you continue your journey.
        <</if>>
    <</if>>
    <<if Weather.dayState is "night">>
        The unlit rural road keeps you jumpy, and the strain of watching every shadow leaves your shoulders tight. <<stress 3>><<gstress>><<set $bikeDurability -= 1>><br><br>
    <</if>>
    <<if Time.season is "spring">>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
            Muddy run-off cuts across the road in shallow streams, forcing you to grind through patches that tug at your wheels. <<stress 4>><<gstress>><<set $bikeDurability -= 3>>
        <<else>>
            The road is rough from winter damage, and every hidden rut jars the frame and your wrists. <<tiredness 3>><<gtiredness>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif Time.season is "summer">>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
            The open road offers no shelter from the downpour, and puddles force you to keep wrestling the handlebars straight. <<stress 4>><<gstress>><<set $bikeDurability -= 3>>
        <<else>>
            Heat shimmers over the asphalt and the long exposed ride slowly drains your energy.<<tiredness 5>><<gtiredness>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif Time.season is "autumn">>
        Crosswinds, grit, and damp leaves make the countryside ride feel longer and rougher than it should.<<tiredness 6>><<gtiredness>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 2>>
    <<elseif Time.season is "winter">>
        The cold wind across the fields cuts right through you, and the frozen road punishes both your body and the bike. <<stress 4>><<gstress>><<set $bikeDurability -= 3>>
    <</if>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain" or $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain">>
        The sun shines brightly while riding with your bike through the open landscape. A big swarm of flies appears in eyesight buzzing your way. You swirl out of the way of the incoming swarm just on time. <<stress -2>><<llstress>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain" or $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain">>
        The open landscape passes by while riding through it with your bike. Suddenly a loud honk from a passing car scares the living hell out of you. With your eyes locked at the car and cursing in yourself you don't notice the black mass of flies directly ahead. 
        When you do notice it is already too late. The swarm surrounds your head and flies start to fly into your mouth. After the swarm is gone, you try to spit out as much of it as you can, but a bitter taste remains in your mouth for a long time. <<stress 12>><<gggstress>><<arousal -300>><<larousal>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation is "rain" or $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 85 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
        The skies are cloudy and rain falls down to the ground at a fast rate. Already the drains are overflowing and forming deep streams next to the bicycle path. 
        Slippery as it is, you manage to stay on your bike for the whole ride. <<stress -2>><<llstress>> <<control 1>> <<gcontrol>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "summer" and Weather.precipitation is "rain" or $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "spring" and Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
    While riding with your bike, pouring rain is coming out of the clouds above you. Visibility is almost non-existent and the bicycle path is slippery. 
    A loud screeching sound comes from behind you. You look and see a big truck slipping hard on the road, some of his wheels already on the bicycle path. 
    <br>
    Instinctively you turn your bike to the right and crash in a field full of high grass and full of deep puddles from the rain. The trucker gets his grip again and drives by, ignoring you entirely. <<pain 4>><<gpain>><<control -2>><<lcontrol>> <<trauma 3>><<gtrauma>> <<upperwet 30>> <<underupperwet 30>> <<lowerwet 30>> <<underlowerwet 30>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 25>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 86 and $rng lte 89 and (Time.season is "summer" or Time.season is "spring") and Weather.precipitation isnot "rain">>
        The heat shimmers off the open road. With no shade for miles, the sun beats down relentlessly. Sweat drips into your eyes and your legs start to cramp. You arrive exhausted and parched. <<tiredness 6>><<gtiredness>><<set $bikeDurability -= 5>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 86 and $rng lte 89 and (Time.season is "summer" or Time.season is "spring") and Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
        A passing lorry clips a deep puddle and sends a wall of muddy water crashing over you. Blinded and sputtering, you swerve and your chain slips off the gears with a sickening clunk. You have to stop and fix it with filthy, shaking hands. <<stress 6>><<ggstress>><<upperwet 70>> <<underupperwet 70>> <<lowerwet 70>> <<underlowerwet 70>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 18>> <<control -1>><<lcontrol>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 80 and Time.season is "autumn">>
        Strong crosswinds batter you on the exposed farmland road. Fallen leaves swirl around your wheels, and the constant fight to stay straight leaves your arms aching. <<stress 4>><<gstress>> <<tiredness 6>><<gtiredness>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 5>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 81 and $rng lte 89 and Time.season is "autumn">>
        <<if Weather.precipitation is "rain">>
        Autumn rain has turned the road shoulder into a mud slick. A tractor rumbles past, spraying you with a wave of muddy water. Blinded, you ride straight into a ditch and go over the handlebars. <<stress 7>><<ggstress>> <<pain 4>><<gpain>><<set $bikeDurability -= 20>> <<upperwet 20>> <<underupperwet 20>> <<lowerwet 20>> <<underlowerwet 20>>
        <<else>>
        A sudden gust of autumn wind catches you broadside on the open road. You swerve hard, your tire catches a rut, and you crash onto the gravel shoulder, scraping your side raw. <<stress 6>><<ggstress>> <<pain 4>><<gpain>><<set $bikeDurability -= 15>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "autumn">>
        The road is a mess of mud, leaves, and standing water from days of rain. A truck barrels past too close, its wake shoving you off the road entirely. You crash through a fence into a waterlogged field, your bike frame bending on impact. You lie in the cold mud, stunned and hurting.<<pain 6>><<ggpain>> <<trauma 4>><<gtrauma>> <<control -3>><<lcontrol>><<upperwet 40>> <<underupperwet 40>> <<lowerwet 40>> <<underlowerwet 40>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 30>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 71 and $rng lte 80 and Time.season is "winter">>
        <<if Weather.isSnow>>
        Snow drifts pile across the farmland road, forcing you to dismount and push through the deepest sections. By the time the road clears, your legs are burning and your clothes are soaked from the knees down.<<stress 4>><<gstress>> <<lowerwet 60>> <<underlowerwet 60>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 5>>
        <<else>>
        Bitter wind whips across the open farmland, cutting through your clothes. Your fingers go numb and your grip on the handlebars weakens dangerously. <<stress 5>><<gstress>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 81 and $rng lte 89 and Time.season is "winter">>
        <<if Weather.isSnow>>
        Compacted snow hides a patch of ice where the road dips. Your tires spin uselessly and you crash sideways, the frozen ground unforgiving against your body. <<stress 6>><<ggstress>> <<pain 5>><<gpain>> <<control -2>><<lcontrol>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 20>> <<upperwet 40>> <<lowerwet 40>>
        <<else>>
        Black ice stretches across the exposed farmland road. You don't even see it coming. One moment you're pedaling, the next you're sliding across frozen tarmac on your back, your bike skidding away from you. <<stress 7>><<ggstress>> <<pain 5>><<gpain>> <<control -3>><<lcontrol>> <<set $bikeDurability -= 20>>
        <</if>>
    <<elseif $rng gte 90 and Time.season is "winter">>
        A blizzard-like squall descends on the open road. Visibility drops to nothing, wind threatens to rip you off the bike, and a sheet of ice sends you careening into a frozen drainage ditch. The impact jars your entire body. You lie shivering in the ditch, battered and struggling to pull yourself and your mangled bike out. <<pain 8>><<ggpain>> <<trauma 6>><<ggtrauma>> <<control -4>><<lcontrol>><<set $bikeDurability -= 35>>
    <</if>>

<<else>>
    <<bikeError>>
<</if>>
<br><br>

You arrive at your destination.
<br><br>
<<destinationBike>>
